      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update airflow to 3.3.1-2 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-54284 (GHSA-pwgv-4x5q-6m9f): sqlparse's TokenList.__init__ materializes the value of its whole subtree for every group, so crafted SQL causes a CPU denial of service before the depth and token limits apply; it affects sqlparse 0.5.5 and earlier and is fixed in 0.6.0: https://github.com/andialbrecht/sqlparse/security/advisories/GHSA-pwgv-4x5q-6m9f. Listed the files of every published airflow build in the DHI Debian repository, 3.3.0-0 to the current 3.4.0-7 (48 builds, amd64 and arm64; no debug-symbol packages are published for this source), including the members of the wheel, jar and zip archives inside them, and read the sqlparse version from its dist-info metadata under /usr/lib/airflow/lib/python3.13/site-packages; both architectures agree for every build, and no other copy of sqlparse (a second dist-info directory, a vendored package directory or an embedded wheel) is present in any build. Builds 3.3.0-0 to 3.3.1-1 ship sqlparse 0.5.5. From 3.3.1-2 every build ships a fixed release: 0.6.0 in 3.3.1-2 to 3.3.2-19, and 0.6.1 in 3.4.0-0 to 3.4.0-7. So 3.3.1-2 is the first fixed build."
    },
